00:10:04.869 --> 00:10:07.366
was dating Pocahontas and they were

00:10:07.366 --> 00:10:10.274
known as a couple as Johanntes.

00:10:10.430 --> 00:10:11.429
(person speaking indistinctly offscreen)

00:10:11.429 --> 00:10:13.249
Johan said there's a real baseball player,

00:10:13.249 --> 00:10:16.053
leftie, and Pocahontas
is obviously Pocahontas.

00:10:16.223 --> 00:10:17.214
Okay, let's go to it.

00:10:17.406 --> 00:10:20.037
(laughing offscreen)

00:10:22.087 --> 00:10:23.705
Obviously, this is.

00:10:23.705 --> 00:10:25.481
(laughing)

00:10:25.481 --> 00:10:26.923
I got it, Johannes.

00:10:26.923 --> 00:10:27.865
Right?

00:10:27.865 --> 00:10:29.270
- [Voiceover] (mumbles)

00:10:29.270 --> 00:10:31.104
(laughing)

00:10:31.104 --> 00:10:34.621
This is the best question
because the truth is

00:10:34.621 --> 00:10:37.849
I really believe that I'm a bridge, right?

00:10:37.849 --> 00:10:40.008
I'm pulling equally, very aggressively

00:10:40.008 --> 00:10:41.157
from both sides.

00:10:41.157 --> 00:10:43.316
That I'm a human contradiction.

00:10:43.316 --> 00:10:44.733
That if you really watch this show

00:10:44.733 --> 00:10:46.114
and it throws people off,

00:10:46.114 --> 00:10:47.949
as they get deeper into my content,

00:10:47.949 --> 00:10:49.678
that oftentimes I'm saying things

00:10:49.678 --> 00:10:51.838
that contradict themselves
'cause the truth is

00:10:51.838 --> 00:10:54.914
they both live in real
life at the same time

00:10:54.914 --> 00:10:57.352
and it's about finding
that cadence and balance

00:10:57.352 --> 00:10:58.432
to guide through.

00:10:58.432 --> 00:11:02.913
I am massively, at a
global level, patient.

00:11:02.913 --> 00:11:06.186
But on a practical level,
and an execution level,

00:11:06.186 --> 00:11:07.915
I'm very fast, right?

00:11:07.915 --> 00:11:11.712
So it's really, it really is
religion and church, right?

00:11:11.712 --> 00:11:13.825
Like at the highest,
like at the theoretical,

00:11:13.825 --> 00:11:18.514
at the, at the grey levels
of patient, long game,

00:11:18.514 --> 00:11:20.465
I'm aware that as long as I'm alive,

00:11:20.465 --> 00:11:22.113
I'm playing the businessman game

00:11:22.113 --> 00:11:24.412
and it doesn't end tomorrow

00:11:24.412 --> 00:11:25.030
and if it ends tomorrow,

00:11:25.030 --> 00:11:26.992
I don't know the outcome
anyway 'cause I'm dead.

00:11:26.992 --> 00:11:27.537
Right?

00:11:27.537 --> 00:11:29.395
And so, but in real life,

00:11:29.395 --> 00:11:30.672
I understand it's a race

00:11:30.672 --> 00:11:34.433
and speed is a variable for
success to me in a big way.

00:11:34.433 --> 00:11:35.617
Hustle, and so like they're,

00:11:35.617 --> 00:11:37.811
patience and speed are very much

00:11:37.811 --> 00:11:39.157
rubbing against each other

00:11:39.157 --> 00:11:41.235
but it's like the diamond
comes from that, right?

00:11:41.235 --> 00:11:44.556
And so that's the thing
that I think about.

00:11:44.556 --> 00:11:47.911
I find it very easy to do both.

00:11:47.911 --> 00:11:50.476
You have to understand, there's people

00:11:50.476 --> 00:11:55.258
that are both in practical
and philosophical terms,

00:11:55.654 --> 00:11:56.782
and they have different outcomes.

00:11:56.782 --> 00:12:00.067
AKA there's people that philosophically

00:12:00.067 --> 00:12:01.600
are not patient.

00:12:01.600 --> 00:12:02.900
They're impatient.

00:12:02.900 --> 00:12:04.363
And they're fast.

00:12:04.363 --> 00:12:07.845
And they look like the bad
version of what I am, right?

00:12:07.845 --> 00:12:09.865
They're like hustlers and they're like

00:12:09.865 --> 00:12:11.978
doing everything for themselves

00:12:11.978 --> 00:12:12.883
and they're not patient.

00:12:12.883 --> 00:12:14.079
They don't care about the long game

00:12:14.079 --> 00:12:15.263
and they're just gonna take

00:12:15.263 --> 00:12:17.121
and they're just gonna
take and take and take

00:12:17.121 --> 00:12:18.445
and gonna take fast

00:12:18.445 --> 00:12:19.338
and they're gonna gather

00:12:19.338 --> 00:12:22.658
and I think that society,
the game rewards them

00:12:22.658 --> 00:12:24.725
and there's a lot of
millionaires and billionaires

00:12:24.725 --> 00:12:26.536
that didn't do it the right way

00:12:26.536 --> 00:12:27.963
and that's what I think they look like.

00:12:27.963 --> 00:12:29.577
Then there's a lot of people that are

00:12:29.577 --> 00:12:32.097
massively patient and slow,

00:12:32.097 --> 00:12:35.323
and those are the
enormous amount of people

00:12:35.323 --> 00:12:37.518
that, you know, in a business context,

00:12:37.518 --> 00:12:38.238
not in life,

00:12:38.238 --> 00:12:40.258
they're probably some of the loveliest

00:12:40.258 --> 00:12:42.022
human beings that have ever been made

00:12:42.022 --> 00:12:44.483
because they're slow and they're patient

00:12:44.483 --> 00:12:45.481
and everything's just lovely

00:12:45.481 --> 00:12:46.934
and let's just like sit on the porch

00:12:46.934 --> 00:12:48.895
and, you know, drink peach tea

00:12:48.895 --> 00:12:51.414
for the rest of our
lives and like go slow.

00:12:51.414 --> 00:12:52.377
Just go real slow.

00:12:52.377 --> 00:12:54.119
Like let's sit and look at stuff.

00:12:54.119 --> 00:12:57.137
Like let's sit on the porch and look.

00:12:57.137 --> 00:12:58.321
Like look at stuff.

00:12:58.321 --> 00:13:00.132
Like a car just drove by.

00:13:00.132 --> 00:13:00.979
Great.

00:13:00.979 --> 00:13:03.220
Like I mean that, you know,

00:13:03.220 --> 00:13:05.901
is not interesting to me, either,

00:13:05.901 --> 00:13:07.434
and so that exists.

00:13:07.434 --> 00:13:10.313
So I actually think
what I do exists a lot.

00:13:10.313 --> 00:13:14.260
I think it's the likable,
you know, aggressive person.

00:13:14.260 --> 00:13:15.456
And that's, you know, they're out there

00:13:15.456 --> 00:13:17.359
and there's a lot of winners
that are good people.

00:13:17.359 --> 00:13:18.196
I really think that.

00:13:18.196 --> 00:13:20.157
If you look at my analogies,

00:13:20.157 --> 00:13:22.596
the speed part is really valuable, right?

00:13:22.596 --> 00:13:27.280
Like if you're speedy and
selfish and impatient,

00:13:27.634 --> 00:13:29.851
you know, I think the other thing about

00:13:29.851 --> 00:13:32.893
the lack of patience and fast,

00:13:32.893 --> 00:13:34.076
you don't have to be a bad person.

00:13:34.076 --> 00:13:36.213
I think it leads to mistakes.

00:13:36.213 --> 00:13:36.794
Right?

00:13:36.794 --> 00:13:38.476
That's another variable layer here.

00:13:38.476 --> 00:13:40.009
You know, it's funny that my brain

00:13:40.009 --> 00:13:41.355
went that first narrative.

00:13:41.355 --> 00:13:42.494
Here's a second narrative.

00:13:42.494 --> 00:13:45.071
You're going fast, you're not patient,

00:13:45.071 --> 00:13:46.487
so you rush the outcome

00:13:46.487 --> 00:13:48.170
and you leave money on the table.

00:13:48.170 --> 00:13:49.876
You sold a company too soon.

00:13:49.876 --> 00:13:52.408
You weren't as profitable

00:13:52.408 --> 00:13:54.311
as you could've been
because you missed things

00:13:54.311 --> 00:13:57.109
'cause you didn't see it
'cause you weren't tactful.

00:13:57.109 --> 00:14:01.980
And so, you know, I think
it has essence of strategy.

00:14:03.030 --> 00:14:05.406
You know, somebody once said

00:14:05.818 --> 00:14:07.513
to me about Vayner,

00:14:07.513 --> 00:14:09.277
"Gary, you guys are so interesting."

00:14:09.277 --> 00:14:11.008
He was trying to zing me a little bit,

00:14:11.008 --> 00:14:12.552
that we weren't strategic enough.

00:14:12.552 --> 00:14:13.677
He said, "You're so interesting,"

00:14:13.677 --> 00:14:16.115
but he's like, "When
you get into the house,

00:14:16.115 --> 00:14:17.509
"I feel like a lot of times you guys

00:14:17.509 --> 00:14:19.029
"just run through the glass window

00:14:19.029 --> 00:14:20.705
"instead of opening the door."

00:14:20.705 --> 00:14:22.106
It was a funny analogy.

00:14:22.106 --> 00:14:23.811
And then I looked at him and said,

00:14:23.811 --> 00:14:25.633
"Yeah, but we're gonna own all the homes."

00:14:25.633 --> 00:14:26.204
(laughing offscreen)

00:14:26.204 --> 00:14:27.734
I guess that's a good way to end it.

00:14:27.734 --> 00:14:28.859
- [India] That's good.

00:14:29.832 --> 00:14:30.546
- Cool.

